# The two quantitative components, on the screens that have something to measure.
#
# A meter answers "how far along"; these answer "where does this sit on a scale I do not carry
# around". Both are the same argument as the airtime bar's - a length is compared against the
# track it is in, which is right there - taken to the readings that have absolute ends.

scene demo
scale 4
delay 220

# The Nodes list: the trailing column is a signal staircase on every node we heard ourselves,
# and the old "Nhop" or "mqtt" on every node we did not. That split is the point - an SNR from a
# relayed packet describes the relay, so those rows have no signal of their own to draw.
tab nodes
hold 1200

# Foxtrot Mobile: a handheld on a weak link with a battery running down, which is the node that
# puts every band on one screen. Watch the notches rather than the fills: the battery bar is red
# because it is past a mark that is drawn where it actually is, not because a threshold nobody
# can see was crossed.
key down 6
key a
key down 26
hold 1600
key b

# Alfa Ridge: the same rows resting. Same scales, same marks, nothing over a boundary - so the
# two screens are readable against each other rather than each against its own colour.
key down 1
key a
key down 26
hold 1600
key b

# And the airtime bar the band came from, climbing past both of its marks.
tab status
airtime 8 2
hold 700
airtime 31 11
hold 700
airtime 58 19
hold 1400
